lines=['# Empirical repository discrimination through specialization','', 'Do response differences repeat on other issues, and does that repetition justify a repository-specific localization policy? **This panel shows useful response contrasts, but does not validate specialization as the strongest deployment default.** The fixed Studio recipe with explicit Qwen fallback remains better overall. The primary shrinkage selector helps React and recovers much of the Studio benefit on Renovate/Pino, but its errors on other repositories erase the aggregate advantage over Studio.','', 'These are cross-fitted results on previously exposed data. Each of85 independent issue groups contributes once per procedure; repeated configurations, subset fits and shuffles are not independent observations. No outcome-driven refinement was performed.','', '## Verdicts','', '| Question | Evidence | Verdict |','|---|---|---|', '| Repeatable response differences |42 informative calibration/held episodes; median tie-aware response correlation0.253;43 constant profiles uninformative. Within-repository issue variance exceeds between-repository variance. | Some repeated response contrasts; small, heterogeneous panel, no unique fingerprint claim. |', '| Held-out specialization value | Primary67.7110% vs Qwen63.8909%, pooled66.9431%, fixed Studio fallback70.0004%. | Gains over Qwen and learned pooled default; loses2.2894pp to strongest fixed default. |', '| Own versus transferred profiles | Own-minus-other donor+0.7230pp; completed calibratable refit+0.2411pp; leave-one-repository-out advantage changes sign. | General own-profile advantage unresolved; concrete preference reversals remain descriptive. |', '| Simpler-policy sufficiency | Imports-only selector63.7653%; primary67.7110%; local65.9555%. | Simple calibrated imports do not retain the main useful call/import distinctions here; conventional Studio still wins. |', '| Availability |47/85 structural completions;14 observed groups,12 with≥2 completed issues;38 fallbacks under primary/Studio. | Failure recovery contributes operational utility; eight all-fallback repositories are structurally unmeasured. |', '| Cost and correctness |11,656 exact native profile checks;26,837 rank/metric checks;174 independently recomputed payloads exact; five scratch mutation/rollback checks pass. | Deterministic replay and supervision isolation verified; marginal selected-pattern extraction/join cost unavailable. |', '', '## Population, admission and evidence','', 'Inherited `nebius/SWE-rebench-V2`, revision `10483de0f50fe5da545942705a76c6150171af7f`, parquet `data/train-00000-of-00001.parquet`, SHA256 `0e0bf9355f892ad74ae98d4e1c404f39fd6654a8e351ee3e6ab162e4a64cd3ad`. The localization-attune-panel-2026-10-06 has96 retained tasks/24 groups/92 source worlds. This experiment uses85 eligible tasks/22 groups/81 worlds with valid inherited Qwen predictions;41 single-file and44 multi-file tasks. Sources are snapshots, not81 independent repositories. All96 entries and exclusions remain in the sealed split manifest.','', 'Dataset patches, repository origins and base revisions were verified directly. Duplicate-patch/query and predeclared near-duplicate checks found85 independent groups, no related pairs. Four issue pairs share a world; leave-world-out results are identical here. Commit/issue order and `created_at` do not establish resolution or label availability. The temporal companion is `ReferenceUnavailable`, not guessed. Additional catalogue issues for these origins are inventoried separately, but lack validated retained acquisition and were not added.','', 'The same current admission version,64 executed native patterns and595 frozen configurations are reused. No source/resolver repair, inference call, pattern enumeration, new fusion scale, or outcome-specific repository exception was introduced. Native witnesses preserve the old nominal-symbol contract; that contract does not establish correct source binding. Pruned extraction worldsw34,w35,w41,w84 remain pruned.36 eligible admission/parser failures and two eligible extraction timeouts remain visible.','', 'The inherited strict account is unchanged: Qwen63.8909%, Studio42.9928%; common completed Qwen62.4238%, Studio73.8102%. New fallback v1 returns exact Qwen only on unavailable/invalid selected execution, preserving state, reasons and attempted cost. A completed empty pattern follows its original empty behavior. Invalid Qwen refuses. No failure becomes an empty successful graph.','', '## Held-out policies','', 'Four synchronized identity-balanced slots leave one independent issue per repository out where present. Flix fits only physically separated allowed calibration rows. Primary estimates use fixed shrinkage strength2 and repository-equal pooling from other repositories; secondary uses local effects only. Qwen/Identity remain candidates. Calibration MRR, primitive-atom cost and deterministic identity break ties; unavailable marginal timing is not a tie-break. Profiles seal before recipient application, and held labels first enter the evaluator.','', '| Procedure | Macro Recall@10 | Macro MRR@10 | Macro FileAcc@10 | Micro Recall@10 | Fallback tasks |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
